  "test_driven_corrections": "The initial constructor-only scope assertion correctly rejected the second MatLegacyTabLink constructor in the nav file. Inspecting that constructor exposed the missing NewExpression inventory; an expected16 check then correctly revealed the separate chip construction as well. Both exact call sites were inspected before setting the finite17 roster. Tab-link construction and its trigger-setup argument are now covered with an explicit renderer protocol; chips remain a behavior-owner review, not a new admission.",
  "review_boundary": "Only the public NgZone import/type and exact caller-object forwarding in these seven source files is admitted. Every construction phase, parameter/field initialization and actual parent/renderer argument is reconciled to the independent historical constructor. Genuine original/current public zones and public zoneless providers execute. Parent and renderer services are recording protocols; their methods/callbacks/lifecycle, Angular decorators/factories/legacy node DI, AOT/packed/native/consumer and full floors are not qualified. The18 other frozen NgZone behavior-owner imports remain open.",
